# g45-fu-rest core wiring

## 1. compose_flip.rs: one reader of a session's attachments
The blob domain's `attachment` transfer source and the desktop residual service now read through ONE type: SessionAttachmentLinks is deleted
(its rule was the same as desktop_residual::session_attachments, over thread items instead of display rows) and DesktopAttachmentHost implements
`SessionAttachments` as well as `AttachmentHost`. In the `PostSeams { ... }` of the "10b. the post-directory domain stage" replace

    session_attachments: Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::attachments::SessionAttachmentLinks::new(directory.clone())),

with

    session_attachments: Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::attachments::DesktopAttachmentHost::new(directory.clone(), blobs.clone(), &b.tokens)),

(`blobs` and `b.tokens` are already in scope there: the DesktopResidualService registration below uses them). The build fails at that line until this is applied.

## 2. SERVICE_PENDING
No change: no core service is added (the new request `host/browser/ref/mint` is a host request the engine sends, like `host/browser/ref/call`).

## 3. Cargo
No new dependency edge: mixdog-ssh already depends on mixdog-rt (`mixdog_rt::time::sleep`/`timeout` used by the callback forward and `SshTunnel::ready`);
mixdog-browser-engine uses mixdog-js already.

## 4. Protocol
See pending-rows/g45-fu-rest.rows (host/browser/ref/mint, frameOffset, observation, read offset, geometry pinInset doc). The engine crate needs them to compile.
The runner that builds the page's ref set from a snapshot result (s4-engine-runner) calls `RefSet::from_payload(..).with_document(..).with_observation(result.observation.as_deref())`
and the reply baseline is `EffectBaseline::of(&set)`; the runner also builds `EngineSinkImpl::new(lane.mirror().clone(), lane.hold().clone())` (the lane owns the
person's holds and lets go of a page it closes) and implements `FilePort::write_frame(run_dir, bytes, mime_type) -> io::Result<PathBuf>` (the file name follows the mime type;
a write that fails leaves the picture inline).
